Laws of Agents, Halachah 3 — Part 4 (§§16–20)

Likutay Halachos, Choshen Mishpat. Based on Likutay Moharan I:51 ("Amar Rabbi Akiva").

Translated from the Hebrew.

And this is: "You wept a weeping for nothing; I will establish for you a weeping for generations." "Weeping" specifically — for it is drawn through sheker [falsehood], which damages the sight of the eyes, as above. And therefore one needs to weep over the destruction of the Bais HaMikdash [Holy Temple]. And likewise one who wants to return in truth needs to weep over his sins before Hashem Yisbarach and to request from before Him that He should grant him to draw close to Him, Yisbarach, in truth. As it is written (Yirmiyahu 31:8): "Bivchi yavo'u uvisachnunim ovilaim," etc. ["With weeping they shall come and with supplications I shall lead them"].
